  "body": "Found during the review fix of PR #3353 (#3316).\n\n**What happens.** A 2D pocket plan with more than one pass in one area re-enters each pass whose start is still in material by the user's entry (`entry_restart`, #2265). Two such helices can stand side by side. Their arcs then cross in XY at a shared depth, and `verify::crossed_pairs` names the pair.\n\n**Where it shows.** `crates/motion/tests/pass_start_levels.rs`, the band case (stock 84 x 24, a round part of radius 15, tool radius 4, Helix entry radius 1.5):\n- Outside, step 3: the first descent helix (moves 2-5) and the next re-entry helix (moves 16-19) cross.\n- Inside, step 4: moves 3/5 and 13/15 cross.\n\nThe test `the_start_side_plan_posts_no_crossing_feeds` checks only the planar feeds for this reason.\n\n**Not a gouge.** Both helices stay in the certified area. The second one bores where the first one cut already. The defect is the warning that the user sees, and an entry that does not use the cut column.\n\n**Done means.** A re-entry whose helix would overlap an earlier helix at the same depth uses that cleared column (or moves its site), and the crossing law finds no helix pair. A test pins the band case above.\n",
